From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Qianzhou Wang <wangqianzhou@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 23:55:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] serial: qcom-geni: acknowledge IRQs during the suspend window

serial_core sets uart_port::suspended before calling the driver's
shutdown callback. The qcom-geni interrupt handler currently returns
IRQ_NONE while that flag is set, without acknowledging any latched
interrupt status. If an RX or DMA interrupt arrives before shutdown has
masked the IRQ, the level-triggered line remains asserted and genirq can
eventually disable it as unhandled. The port then cannot communicate
after resume.

The serial engine remains powered until shutdown has disabled the IRQ
and uart_change_pm() has run. Acknowledge all four interrupt status
registers in this narrow transition window and report the interrupt as
handled. Normal suspended operation is unchanged because shutdown masks
the IRQ before the runtime power transition.

Signed-off-by: Qianzhou Wang <wangqianzhou@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
index 4d7156b11483..0882096ab47c 100644
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
@@ -1071,8 +1071,26 @@ static irqreturn_t qcom_geni_serial_isr(int isr, void *dev)
 	struct tty_port *tport = &uport->state->port;
 	struct qcom_geni_serial_port *port = to_dev_port(uport);
 
-	if (uport->suspended)
-		return IRQ_NONE;
+	/*
+	 * serial_core marks the port suspended before ->shutdown() masks the
+	 * IRQ. If a level-triggered RX or DMA interrupt arrives in that window,
+	 * returning IRQ_NONE leaves the status latched and genirq may disable
+	 * the line as unhandled. The hardware is still powered until shutdown
+	 * completes, so drain the pending status before returning.
+	 */
+	if (uport->suspended) {
+		m_irq_status = readl(uport->membase + SE_GENI_M_IRQ_STATUS);
+		s_irq_status = readl(uport->membase + SE_GENI_S_IRQ_STATUS);
+		dma_tx_status = readl(uport->membase + SE_DMA_TX_IRQ_STAT);
+		dma_rx_status = readl(uport->membase + SE_DMA_RX_IRQ_STAT);
+
+		writel(m_irq_status, uport->membase + SE_GENI_M_IRQ_CLEAR);
+		writel(s_irq_status, uport->membase + SE_GENI_S_IRQ_CLEAR);
+		writel(dma_tx_status, uport->membase + SE_DMA_TX_IRQ_CLR);
+		writel(dma_rx_status, uport->membase + SE_DMA_RX_IRQ_CLR);
+
+		return IRQ_HANDLED;
+	}
 
 	uart_port_lock(uport);
 
-- 
